          "reasoning": "@Response 2 is better than @Response 1.  Both response provide an alternate ending when Asuka is not killed, however @Response 2 is preferred because it engages more of the original story which makes the alternate ending fit seamlessly into the script. ",
          "feedback1": "The response is partially helpful.  This response is considered just partially helpful because it does not address part of the instructions in the prompt.  It does provide an alternate ending with Asuka not dying because Shinji is there with her.  However, it does not mention the reason Asuka needs to be saved from the EVAs that reanimated after she beat them and then kill her by disemboweling her. ",
          "feedback2": "The response is mostly helpful.  This response is mostly helpful because while providing a well constructed alternate ending it does so by taking over from the precise moment that Asuka is about to be killed by the Mass Productions Evangelions.  If this response would have included the Shunji arrives immediately after Asuka has defeated the EVAs and they reanimate. "
        },
